<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Astana</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Akmola, Tselinograd, Nur-Sultan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Astana is the capital of Kazakhstan, on the Ishim River in the north of the country. Founded as the Russian fort of Akmolinsk in 1830, it was renamed Tselinograd during the Virgin Lands campaign and became the capital in 1997. It was called Nur-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> from 2019 to 2022, and is known for its modern government buildings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/astana.jpg" alt="Astana" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dauren Nabijan · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Astana_Esil_view.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
